  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Securing Rights of Women Domestic Workers in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will build the capacity of 06 organizations to undertake their ongoing roles in promoting and protecting the rights of women domestic workers. The initiative will directly benefit 16000 women domestic workers, and indirectly benefit members of their households, particularly their children.  The project will also indirectly benefit other women domestic workers (including migrant domestic workers), child domestic workers, employers, and community members. By its completion, the project will have achieved two key outcomes: women domestic workers in Dhaka will be better empowered and organized to claim and defend their rights, particularly their right to live free from violence; and Bangladeshi society, government and employers will increase their support for protecting the rights of women domestic workers.</narrative>
  </description>
